  "risk_register": [
    "Changing n_steps from 512 to 256 changes per-environment GAE segmentation even though the total 2048-transition rollout is preserved; C0 controls this common change but does not make it identical to the source optimisation process.",
    "Changing the training episode horizon from 600 to 512 is common to C0 and C1 but remains a continuation-distribution change.",
    "Flat training makes the 13D terrain preview nearly constant and can cause terrain-skill forgetting; the final standard-slope continuity gate is therefore mandatory.",
    "Worker magnitude is confounded with worker rank in this minimal pilot; opposite phases and within-worker sign alternation remove direction exposure imbalance but do not fully randomise magnitude across seed streams.",
    "A successful C1 result supports the whole balanced-command intervention; it cannot by itself isolate policy weights from contact asymmetry, actuator ordering or initial-state effects.",
    "The low-speed conditions remain positive-speed out-of-training-envelope probes and are not in-place rotation tests."
  ],
  "claim_boundary": "This paired protocol can test whether one short, exactly counterbalanced flat-command continuation repairs the observed closed-loop yaw asymmetry while retaining predeclared safety and standard-slope floors. It cannot establish causal mechanism, true in-place turning, fixed-map readiness, route optimality, random-map generalisation, natural gait, electrical-energy improvement or promotion."
